2026-08-28 — deploy: 20260828190000_a_poke_never_waits_for_a_lock.sql.
             poke_worker claimed its throttle slot with `on conflict do
             update`, which takes a row lock — so two people posting a photo in
             the same second serialised on one row, on the path of SENDING A
             MESSAGE. Short in practice, and the failure mode is bad in a
             specific way: a wait long enough to hit statement_timeout raises
             query_canceled, which plpgsql's `when others` does not catch, so
             the handler that exists to keep a poke harmless would let it
             through and the insert would fail. A try-advisory lock removes the
             wait entirely; losing that race is the same answer the throttle
             gives anyway. create-or-replace — the signature is unchanged and
             four triggers depend on the caller.
